Okay, here's my 2 GP worth:

> 1)  Fancy Mazes
I like them.  For best results, limit use of teleporting and digging wands/
pickaxes/etc on those levels.

> 2)  Reincarnation (rogue-like levels)
I assume this refers to bones levels.  I hate them; ghosts are just about
impossible to kill.  At least, there should be an O)ption to disable them
(possibly with a score penalty).

> 3)  Stronghold levels
The existing game has enough of this.  However, I would like to see more of
the Rogue "treasure zoos" (rooms filled wall-to-wall with monsters and
objects, usually one of each per space).  If you've never been dumped into
one of these by a pit trap, you haven't lived.

> 6)  Seduce (succubi/incubi)
These are too powerful; I don't know any defense against them.  Nuke them or
make it possible to fight them, or at least make them roll to "hit" on you.

> 12) Explore mode
This is a good thing, almost indispensible for new players.  I would add code
to offer this mode as an option after you are killed when playing normally.
(It would take some of the unfairness out of stupid deaths such as starving.)

> 13) Sounds/Music
This is a neat idea in principle, but I don't see any way to write portable
code for it.  If done, it should work on PCs with no sound card (don't tell
me it's impossible, I've got 5 other games that do it now) and should respect
the "silent" option so I can let the neighbors sleep when I play at 2 AM. :)

